Novel-only runtime distribution (alpha.23 development): the official SDK and
CLI remain pinned and use sdk-minimal with novel-only overlays. Selected
unused generic office, voice, inspector and browser payloads are omitted;
upstream module code, manifests and retained notices remain. This is not a
complete general-purpose DSH desktop distribution. Exact resource patterns
are retained in plan/runtime-resource-exclusions.json and runtime inventory.

Editable DOCX export (alpha.24 development) bundles docx 9.14.0 and its
JavaScript runtime dependencies. Retained attribution and complete supplied
licence texts are in licenses/docx-runtime/ with exact-byte provenance.
Microsoft Word and the native LibreOffice QA engine are not distributed as
part of this export feature; user novels retain their authors' own rights.

Incremental backup writer ownership (alpha.27 development) uses Koffi 3.1.1
for fixed Windows CreateFileW/WriteFile/FlushFileBuffers/CloseHandle calls.
The existing exact dependency is now part of the runtime; its unmodified MIT
notice is retained in licenses/vault-runtime/Koffi-LICENSE.txt. No general
native function, filesystem or shell tool is exposed to the novel agent.

